Sub-problem-Id: 4; Sub-problem: What is the absolute difference between \(\pi\) and \(\frac{22}{7}\)?;

Answer: The value of the common fraction \(\frac{22}{7}\) as a decimal is \(3.1428571428...\). Therefore, the absolute difference between \(\pi\) and \(\frac{22}{7}\) is \(|\pi-\frac{22}{7}|=|3.1415926535...-3.1428571428...|=0.0006484283...\).

Please note that this answer will be used in the next sub-problem to solve.
